Reference implementation: SucreRouge/synth_control (Bayesian Robust Synthetic Control)
=====================================================================================

This benchmark cross-validates mlsynth's Bayesian Robust Synthetic Control
posterior -- the ``estimator="bayesian"`` path of ClusterSC's PCR family
(``mlsynth.utils.clustersc_helpers.pcr.bayesian``) -- against an independent
Python reference:

    https://github.com/SucreRouge/synth_control
    Implements: the Bayesian branch of Robust Synthetic Control,
                Amjad, Shah & Shen, "Robust Synthetic Control",
                Journal of Machine Learning Research 19(22):1-51, 2018.

The branch used is ``synth_functions.learn(method="bayesian")``: rank-k hard
singular-value thresholding (HSVT) of the donor matrix, a data-driven prior
precision (a forward-chaining ridge-CV penalty times the inverse pre-period
variance), and the closed-form Gaussian-conjugate posterior over the donor
weights -- unconstrained weights, no intercept, no simplex.

The repository carries no LICENSE file. Rather than vendoring un-licensed source
into mlsynth, the reference is fetched on demand at a pinned commit and imported
from a local cache; nothing from it is redistributed in this tree.

