Dependencies: numpy, scikit-learn, scipy, matplotlib.

Faithfulness note: build_bayesian_rsc (clone_synth_control.py) reproduces
learn(method="bayesian") using the upstream threshold() and forward_chain()
unmodified and the same posterior algebra, so it can return the two data-driven
plug-ins (sigma^2 and the prior precision) the case needs; the algorithm itself
is the upstream source. No modifications are made to the reference source.

What the case pins (see benchmarks/cases/bayesian_rsc_ref.py)
------------------------------------------------------------
mlsynth and this reference compute the IDENTICAL Bayesian RSC posterior:
posterior covariance inv(prior_precision I + (1/sigma^2) A'A) and mean
(1/sigma^2) Sigma A'y. The case denoises the donor matrix with mlsynth's own
HSVT (which reproduces the reference's rank-k truncation to ~1e-12 on this fully
observed panel), feeds mlsynth's BayesSCM the reference's data-driven sigma^2 and
prior precision, and pins that the posterior-mean donor weights, the
counterfactual, and the ATT match the captured reference to ~1e-8.

Convention note. mlsynth's DEFAULT public path (CLUSTERSC estimator="bayesian")
sets sigma^2 from the OLS fit residual and uses a fixed prior precision, not the
reference's total-variance sigma^2 and forward-chaining ridge-CV prior. Those are
deliberate plug-in choices, so the default public path does not reproduce the
reference to 1e-8; the shared object the two implementations agree on is the
posterior kernel and the HSVT denoiser, which is what this case cross-validates,
holding sigma^2 and the prior precision fixed across the two.
